  "__note": "Reviewed semantic-rename rules for aeloria's src/ slices (PLAN §5, campaign run 2026-10-14). Keyed by capture rel; `renames` maps a chunk's top-level binding (top-level declaration or import alias) to a semantic name. tools/apply-names.mjs fires only on identifiers that resolve, through the real scope chain, to the chunk's PROGRAM scope (shadowed locals are untouched), refuses shorthand/property/key/export positions, refuses a name declared in or referenced from an in-chunk wholeFile vendor/machinery region (those regions are never rewritten and carry no records), refuses target collisions and chained renames — vendor identifiers stay minified by construction. Vendor import aliases are renamed only where the app's own usage proves what the export is. The achieved per-file maps are recovered into rename-map.json by tools/recover-scoped-map.mjs and re-checked by tools/verify-rename.mjs, tools/check-chunk.mjs and tools/audit.js. Rules the region guard refuses (shared with the inlined postprocessing region) are recorded in README.md, not here."
